# What the image build does not need.
#
# `node_modules` is excluded rather than copied: the build resolves its own from the lockfile, and copying a
# host's tree would put whatever platform it was installed on into the image.
#
# `.env` is excluded for a stronger reason. This repository reads provider keys and a TYPESAFE_API_KEY from
# the environment, and a checked-out `.env` next to the source would otherwise be baked into a layer — where
# it is not secret any more, whatever the registry's visibility. A container gets its credentials from the
# environment at run time, which is the only place they can be revoked.

.git
.gitignore
.data
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.env
.env.*
*.log
multix-output
plans/reports/evidence
.github
